CloudBurrow patch 63 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1522). Applies after patch 0054.

Patch 0036 gave no change table to a table with any column whose name
starts _CHANGE_ (a query's results may name a change column so), and
patch 0044 left such columns out of the history a CREATE OR REPLACE
carries. BigQuery reserves only the prefixes _CHANGE_TYPE,
_CHANGE_TIMESTAMP and _CHANGE_SEQUENCE_NUMBER
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas, "Column names", read
2026-10-17), which CloudBurrow's front refuses; another column so named,
_CHANGE_NOTE say, is the table's own, and its history is kept as any
table's. The patch leaves out of the change history only a table with a
column of one of the change table's own names (_CHANGE_TYPE,
_CHANGE_TIMESTAMP, _CHANGE_IS_FOR_UPDATE, without case), and carries
every other column.

